{"book":{"id":"book-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman","slug":"kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman","title":"Kennedy's Wars: Berlin, Cuba, Laos, and Vietnam","authors":[{"id":"person-lawrence-freedman","name":"Lawrence Freedman"}],"isbn13":["9780198030751"],"subjects":["War & Military"],"topics":["Vietnam War","Science & Discovery","Cold War & Nuclear Politics","Latin America & the Caribbean"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Kennedy's%20Wars%3A%20Berlin%2C%20Cuba%2C%20Laos%2C%20and%20Vietnam%20Lawrence%20Freedman","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Kennedy's%20Wars%3A%20Berlin%2C%20Cuba%2C%20Laos%2C%20and%20Vietnam%20Lawrence%20Freedman","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Kennedy's%20Wars%3A%20Berlin%2C%20Cuba%2C%20Laos%2C%20and%20Vietnam%20Lawrence%20Freedman","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Kennedy's%20Wars%3A%20Berlin%2C%20Cuba%2C%20Laos%2C%20and%20Vietnam%20Lawrence%20Freedman","publisher":"https://openlibrary.org/works/OL5303930W"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-arthur-ross-international-affairs-wikipedia-arthur-ross-book-award","source-open-library-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman","source-open-library-summary-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman"],"publicationYear":2000,"thumbnailUrl":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/125828-L.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0,"traits":[],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"renownProfile":{"knowsBook":true,"publicFame":35,"criticalRenown":72,"controversy":18,"llmAffinity":76,"affinityResidual":0.19,"confidence":{"publicFame":0.9,"criticalRenown":0.9,"controversy":0.8,"llmAffinity":0.93},"tags":{"craft":"craft-of-explanation","evidence":"archival-research","stance":"revisionism"},"model":"gpt-5.6-luna","promptVersion":1},"summary":"\"In his thousand-day presidency, John F. Kennedy led America through one of its most difficult and potentially explosive eras. With the Cold War at its height and the threat of communist advances in Europe and the Third World, Kennedy had the unenviable task of sustaining political support at home without leading the western world into a nuclear catastrophe.\". \"In Kennedy's Wars, noted historian Lawrence Freedman draws on the best of Cold War scholarship and newly released government documents to illuminate Kennedy's approach to war and his efforts for peace. He recreates insightfully the political and intellectual milieu of the foreign policy establishment during Kennedy's era with vivid profiles of his top advisors - Robert McNamara, Dean Rusk, Robert Kennedy - and influential figures such as Dean Acheson and Walt Rostow. Tracing the evolution of traditional liberalism into the Cold War liberalism of Kennedy's cabinet, Freedman evaluates their responses to the tensions in Berlin, Cuba, Laos, and Vietnam. He gives each conflict individual attention, showing how foreign policy decisions came to be defined for each new crisis in the light of those that had gone before.","subjectCategories":[{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Kennedy, john f. (john fitzgerald), 1917-1963","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United states, foreign relations, 1961-1981","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"United states, military policy","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawrence-freedman"},{"source":"open_library","scheme":"open_library_subject","label":"Cold war","sourceId":"source-open-library-summary-kennedy-s-wars-berlin-cuba-laos-and-vietnam-lawr